Research Gap and Positioning

The reviewed literature shows substantial interest in robust machinery diagnosis under changing operating
conditions. More complex solutions may involve multimodal fusion, causal representation learning, or
adaptation to target-domain data. The present project investigates a more compact question: whether
measured-speed-informed order-domain normalization improves performance relative to raw-signal learning,
and whether a consistency term adds value once order-domain inputs are used. The project is positioned as a
controlled empirical comparison, not as a claim that order tracking or consistency learning is entirely new.
